 {"status": "blocked", "id": "BT-81", "title": "3,761 rows sit outside boardctl's own canonical status vocabulary because validation only WARNS; and 'complete' still cannot be told from 'verified'", "detail": {"fingerprint": "c6da6dc951b6aa28ccb6762f0da4e50239b84d5d5e03b9f47f5e5199fdf26467"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "A migration maps every existing status to the canonical four with zero rows left unmapped; the census and gate read one criteria field with a documented legacy fallback; a board written by either writer produces identical counts; the 12-variant count is zero on a re-scan. Evidence: coding-hermes-boardctl/internal/board/validate.go:67 (canonical vocabulary) and :175 (alias warnings); 3,761 non-canonical rows counted across every tasks.jsonl on 2026-10-28.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": null, "guard_result": null, "ci_result": null, "worker_summary": null, "foreman_note": null, "completed_at": null, "acceptance_criteria": "CORRECTED PREMISE (2026-10-28, after re-reading our own code): internal/board/validate.go already defines the canonical set {pending,in_progress,review,blocked,complete,failed}, already REJECTS aliases on write, already names the canonical value for a known alias as a WARNING, and already ships 'boardctl update <id> --normalize' as the sanctioned fix. So the vocabulary exists and is enforced at the write path - the earlier claim of a missing canonical set was wrong, and the real gap is that the repair sweep never ran. Measured across every board: 320,045 complete and 51,501 pending canonical rows against 3,761 non-canonical rows still on disk (done 1,562, open 794, null 674, closed 473, superseded 91, completed 80, in-progress 27, duplicate 27, added 9, stale 8). Deliver two things. (1) Run the normalization: a re-runnable sweep with a dry-run count that drives the 3,761 alias rows to canonical values through boardctl update --normalize, board by board, and then state whether validate should escalate alias warnings to errors per board so the debt cannot re-accumulate. (2) Add the distinction the vocabulary genuinely lacks: reported-done is not verified. A row closing because a lane stopped and a row closing because evidence was checked are the same value today; add a marker that a report can read and count.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-10-28T04:37:50.054253+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-28T04:58:18.316902+00:00", "acceptance": "Non-canonical status rows fleet-wide reach 0 from 3,761; the sweep is one re-runnable command with a dry-run count; the escalate-or-tolerate policy is documented per board; a reported-vs-verified marker exists and is counted by at least one report.", "blocked_reason": "OWNER: Bane \u2014 fleet-wide vocabulary policy change (canonical set shift from pending/in_progress/blocked/complete to open/in_progress/blocked/closed) requires owner authorization before implementation. Row filed 2026-10-28T04:37:50Z, no foreman_note or review_notes present."}
