one:not-written STATUS: complete TIER: T3 EVIDENCE: go build/vet/test + guard PASS; focused tests PASS; malformed digest rc=1 with tasks.jsonl byte-identical; push parity 0", "completed_at": "2026-10-28 17:45:00", "acceptance_criteria": "internal/board/fingerprint.go already computes FindingFingerprint(title, reasoning) for dedupe and appendEvidenceEvent carries a fingerprint parameter, so the word 'fingerprint' in this repo means 'is this the same issue', not 'are these the same bytes' - DOC-16 already caught status-vocabulary drift from that ambiguity. That conflates two identities and makes evidence uncitable: a row can say it was evidenced but not against what content. Add a distinct, validated evidence reference to the row/event schema: tree_fp (64 hex chars, the digest produced by gitreins), optional artifact list, and the run id; accept it via '--evidence-fingerprint' and '--evidence-artifact' on create and evidence, reject malformed digests by shape rather than silently storing prose, and render it in the row detail so a reader can tell finding identity from tree identity. Keep existing finding-fingerprint behaviour and dedupe untouched, and document the two identities in the README section DF-BOARDCTL-11 already touched.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-10-28T13:50:18.805385+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-28T22:43:28.240539+00:00", "blocked_reason": null, "acceptance": "A row can cite tree_fp (64 hex) plus optional artifacts; malformed digests are rejected by shape; finding-fingerprint dedupe is unchanged; row detail shows both identities distinctly; README documents finding vs tree identity.", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/boardctl-BT-82", "branch": "wt/BT-82"}
